  "question": {
    "text": "If $|\\vec{a}|=4,|\\vec{b}|=2$ and the angle between $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ is $\\pi / 6$ then $(\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b})^2=2$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n48\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n16\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\vec{a}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nnone of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}=|\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}| \\cos \\frac{\\pi}{6}=4 \\times 2 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=4 \\sqrt{3}$\nNow, $(\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b})^2+(\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b})^2=a^2 b^2 \\Rightarrow(\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b})^2+48=16 \\times 4 \\Rightarrow(\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b})^2=16$"
  }
}